From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tcpm: restart partner discovery after a response timeout

When the partner's response to Discover Identity, Discover SVIDs or Discover
Modes (SOP) arrives after tVDMSenderResponse, the VDM state machine times out,
finishes the AMS and never asks again. Discovery stops at that step, so the
partner's alternate modes stay unregistered until the next attach. On a
DisplayPort-over-USB-C connection that is a boot without a picture.

Observed on the Radxa Cubie A7S (HUSB311 as TCPC, source/DFP) with a USB-C
DisplayPort adapter identifying as 05e3:0f01, cold-booted with the Type-C/DP
stack built into the kernel so that PD starts ~1 s after VBUS is switched on.
The adapter normally answers each discovery request within 10-18 ms. In the
failing boots one answer comes after ~50 ms instead -- once Discover Identity:

    [2.905338] PD TX, header: 0x17af                (Discover Identity)
    [2.916531] PD TX complete, status: 0
    [2.946577] AMS DISCOVER_IDENTITY finished       (30 ms: timed out)
    [2.970208] PD RX, header: 0x528f [1]            (the ACK, 53.7 ms late)
    [2.970224] PD TX, header: 0x9b0                 (Not_Supported)

and once, after identity and SVIDs had been answered in time, Discover Modes:

    [3.432733] PD TX, header: 0x1baf                (Discover Modes)
    [3.443935] PD TX complete, status: 0
    [3.485119] AMS DISCOVER_MODES finished          (timed out)
    [3.494922] PD RX, header: 0x268f [1]            (the ACK, 51 ms late)
    [3.494930] PD TX, header: 0xdb0                 (Not_Supported)

with nothing further in either case. Across 18 cold boots before these logs
were taken, 4 came up without a picture.

A timeout is not a refusal. Restart discovery from Discover Identity when one
of the three requests times out on SOP, through the same send_discover path
the collision retry already uses, at most DISCOVER_TIMEOUT_RETRIES times per
attach (reset on attach and on hard reset). svdm_consume_identity() clears the
SVIDs and modes gathered by the interrupted pass. SOP' discovery keeps its
existing handling. The late response itself is not consumed; the restart
obtains fresh ones.

Checked against torvalds/master (2026-09-12): the discovery bookkeeping has
been reworked there (vdm_discovery_state), but a response timeout still ends
discovery without a retry.

Assisted-by: Claude

--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
@@ -271,6 +271,7 @@
 
 #define GET_SINK_CAP_RETRY_MS	100
 #define SEND_DISCOVER_RETRY_MS	100
+#define DISCOVER_TIMEOUT_RETRIES	3
 
 struct pd_mode_data {
 	int svid_index;		/* current SVID index		*/
@@ -491,6 +492,7 @@
 	/* PD state for Vendor Defined Messages */
 	enum vdm_states vdm_state;
 	u32 vdm_retries;
+	u32 discover_timeouts;
 	/* next Vendor Defined Message to send */
 	u32 vdo_data[VDO_MAX_SIZE];
 	u8 vdo_count;
@@ -2682,6 +2684,28 @@
 		break;
 	case VDM_STATE_BUSY:
 		port->vdm_state = VDM_STATE_ERR_TMOUT;
+		/*
+		 * A partner that answers Discover Identity, Discover SVIDs or
+		 * Discover Modes only after tVDMSenderResponse has expired is
+		 * never asked again: discovery stops at that step and the
+		 * partner's alternate modes stay unregistered until the next
+		 * attach. Restart discovery from Discover Identity, a bounded
+		 * number of times; svdm_consume_identity() clears the SVIDs and
+		 * modes gathered so far. The late response itself is not
+		 * consumed.
+		 */
+		if (port->tx_sop_type == TCPC_TX_SOP &&
+		    (port->ams == DISCOVER_IDENTITY ||
+		     port->ams == DISCOVER_SVIDS ||
+		     port->ams == DISCOVER_MODES) &&
+		    port->discover_timeouts < DISCOVER_TIMEOUT_RETRIES) {
+			port->discover_timeouts++;
+			tcpm_log(port, "%s timed out, restarting discovery (%u of %u)",
+				 tcpm_ams_str[port->ams], port->discover_timeouts,
+				 DISCOVER_TIMEOUT_RETRIES);
+			port->send_discover = true;
+			mod_send_discover_delayed_work(port, SEND_DISCOVER_RETRY_MS);
+		}
 		if (port->ams != NONE_AMS)
 			tcpm_ams_finish(port);
 		break;
@@ -4484,6 +4508,7 @@
 
 	port->attached = true;
 	port->send_discover = true;
+	port->discover_timeouts = 0;
 	port->send_discover_prime = false;
 
 	return 0;
@@ -4638,6 +4663,7 @@
 
 	port->attached = true;
 	port->send_discover = true;
+	port->discover_timeouts = 0;
 	port->send_discover_prime = false;
 
 	return 0;
@@ -5455,6 +5481,7 @@
 		tcpm_unregister_altmodes(port);
 		port->nr_sink_caps = 0;
 		port->send_discover = true;
+		port->discover_timeouts = 0;
 		port->send_discover_prime = false;
 		if (port->pwr_role == TYPEC_SOURCE)
 			tcpm_set_state(port, SRC_HARD_RESET_VBUS_OFF,
